    <p>
      Now we use this table to perform more complicated multiplications.
    </p>

    <example>
      <statement>
        <p>
          Calculate <m>324_{\text{5}}\times 3_{\text{5}}</m> first using a chip model and then using the column algorithm.
        </p>
      </statement>

      <solution>
        <p>
          First, put 3 copies of <m>324_{\text{5}}</m> on the chart:
        </p>

        <image width="80%">
          <shortdescription>
          </shortdescription>
          <latex-image>
          <![CDATA[ 
          \begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1.3]
            \draw (0,0) rectangle (8,3.5); 
            \draw (0,3)--(8,3);
            \foreach \x in {2,4,6} \draw (\x,0) -- (\x,3.5);
            \foreach \x/\lab in {1/125s,3/25s,5/5s,7/1s} \draw (\x,3.25) node {\lab};
            \foreach \y in {1,2} \draw[dashed] (0,\y)--(8,\y);
            \foreach \y in {0,1,2} {
              % ones
              \foreach \x in {1,2,3,4} \fill[MaterialBlue] ({6+0.3*\x},{\y*1+0.3}) circle[radius=2.5pt];
              % 5s
              \foreach \x in {1,2} \fill[MaterialBlue] ({4+0.3*\x},{\y*1+0.3}) circle[radius=2.5pt];
              % 25s
              \foreach \x in {1,2,3} \fill[MaterialBlue] ({2+0.3*\x},{\y*1+0.3}) circle[radius=2.5pt];  
            }
            \end{tikzpicture}
          ]]>
          </latex-image>
        </image>

        <p>
          And now bundle the ones, remembering to group in size 5.
        </p>

        <image width="80%">
          <shortdescription>
          </shortdescription>
          <latex-image>
          <![CDATA[ 
          \begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1.3]
            \draw (0,0) rectangle (8,3.5); 
            \draw (0,3)--(8,3);
            \foreach \x in {2,4,6} \draw (\x,0) -- (\x,3.5);
            \foreach \x/\lab in {1/125s,3/25s,5/5s,7/1s} \draw (\x,3.25) node {\lab};
            \foreach \y in {1,2} \draw[dashed] (0,\y)--(8,\y);
            \foreach \y in {0,1,2} {
              % ones
              \foreach \x in {1,2,3,4} \fill[MaterialBlue] ({6+0.3*\x},{\y*1+0.5}) circle[radius=2.5pt];
              % 5s
              \foreach \x in {1,2} \fill[MaterialBlue] ({4+0.3*\x},{\y*1+0.5}) circle[radius=2.5pt];
              % 25s
              \foreach \x in {1,2,3} \fill[MaterialBlue] ({2+0.3*\x},{\y*1+0.5}) circle[radius=2.5pt];  
            }
            % cross out 1s
            \draw[dashed,rounded corners,MaterialRed900] (6.1,0.3) -- (7.4,0.3) -- (7.4,1.7) -- (7,1.7) -- (7,0.8) -- (6.1,0.8) -- cycle; 
            \draw[dashed,rounded corners,MaterialRed900] (6.1,1.3) -- (6.1,2.7) -- (7.4,2.7) -- (7.4,1.8) -- (6.45,1.8) -- (6.45,1.3) -- cycle; 
            \foreach \y in {0,2} {
              \fill[MaterialRed900](5.5,{\y+0.5}) circle[radius=2.5pt];
              \draw[->] (6.1,{\y+0.5}) -- (5.6,{\y+0.5}); 
            }
            % cross out the ones:
            \foreach \y in {0,1,2} {
              \foreach \x in {1,4} \draw[thick] ({6+0.3*\x-0.1},{\y+0.4}) -- ({6+0.3*\x+0.1},{\y+0.6});
            }
            \foreach \y in {0,2} {
  \foreach \x in {2,3} \draw[thick] ({6+0.3*\x-0.1},{\y+0.4}) -- ({6+0.3*\x+0.1},{\y+0.6});
}
\end{tikzpicture}
          ]]>
          </latex-image>
        </image>

        <p>
          Next, we bundle the fives:
        </p>

        <image width="80%">
          <shortdescription>
          </shortdescription>
          <latex-image>
          <![CDATA[ 
            \begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1.3]
            \draw (0,0) rectangle (8,3.5); 
            \draw (0,3)--(8,3);
            \foreach \x in {2,4,6} \draw (\x,0) -- (\x,3.5);
            \foreach \x/\lab in {1/125s,3/25s,5/5s,7/1s} \draw (\x,3.25) node {\lab};
            \foreach \y in {1,2} \draw[dashed] (0,\y)--(8,\y);
            \foreach \y in {0,1,2} {
              % ones
              \foreach \x in {1,2,3,4} \fill[MaterialBlue] ({6+0.3*\x},{\y*1+0.5}) circle[radius=2.5pt];
              % 5s
              \foreach \x in {1,2} \fill[MaterialBlue] ({4+0.3*\x},{\y*1+0.5}) circle[radius=2.5pt];
              % 25s
              \foreach \x in {1,2,3} \fill[MaterialBlue] ({2+0.3*\x},{\y*1+0.5}) circle[radius=2.5pt];  
            }
            % bundle the 1s
            \draw[dashed,rounded corners,MaterialRed900] (6.1,0.3) -- (7.4,0.3) -- (7.4,1.7) -- (7,1.7) -- (7,0.8) -- (6.1,0.8) -- cycle; 
            \draw[dashed,rounded corners,MaterialRed900] (6.1,1.3) -- (6.1,2.7) -- (7.4,2.7) -- (7.4,1.8) -- (6.45,1.8) -- (6.45,1.3) -- cycle; 
            \foreach \y in {0,2} {
              \fill[MaterialRed900](5.5,{\y+0.5}) circle[radius=2.5pt];
              \draw[->] (6.1,{\y+0.5}) -- (5.6,{\y+0.5}); 
            }
            % cross out the ones:
            \foreach \y in {0,1,2} {
              \foreach \x in {1,4} \draw[thick] ({6+0.3*\x-0.1},{\y+0.4}) -- ({6+0.3*\x+0.1},{\y+0.6});
            }
            \foreach \y in {0,2} {
              \foreach \x in {2,3} \draw[thick] ({6+0.3*\x-0.1},{\y+0.4}) -- ({6+0.3*\x+0.1},{\y+0.6});
            }
            % bundle the fives:
            \draw[dashed,rounded corners, MaterialRed900] (4.1,0.2) -- (4.1,2.8) -- (5.7,2.8) -- (5.7,2.3) -- (4.45,2.3) -- (4.45,0.2) -- cycle; 
            \fill[MaterialRed900] (3.5,1.5) circle[radius=2.5pt];
            \draw[->] (4.1,1.5) -- (3.6,1.5);
            % cross out the fives
            \foreach \x in {1,2,5} \draw[thick] ({4+0.3*\x-0.1},2.4) -- ({4+0.3*\x+0.1},2.6);
            \foreach \y in {0,1} {
            \foreach \x in {1} \draw[thick] ({4+0.3*\x-0.1},{\y+0.4}) -- ({4+0.3*\x+0.1},{\y+0.6});
            }
            \end{tikzpicture}
          ]]>
          </latex-image>
        </image>

        <p>
          And then bundle the 25s:
        </p>

        <image width="80%">
          <shortdescription>
          </shortdescription>
          <latex-image>
          <![CDATA[ 
          \begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1.3]
            \draw (0,0) rectangle (8,3.5); 
            \draw (0,3)--(8,3);
            \foreach \x in {2,4,6} \draw (\x,0) -- (\x,3.5);
            \foreach \x/\lab in {1/125s,3/25s,5/5s,7/1s} \draw (\x,3.25) node {\lab};
            \foreach \y in {1,2} \draw[dashed] (0,\y)--(8,\y);
            \foreach \y in {0,1,2} {
              % ones
              \foreach \x in {1,2,3,4} \fill[MaterialBlue] ({6+0.3*\x},{\y*1+0.5}) circle[radius=2.5pt];
              % 5s
              \foreach \x in {1,2} \fill[MaterialBlue] ({4+0.3*\x},{\y*1+0.5}) circle[radius=2.5pt];
              % 25s
              \foreach \x in {1,2,3} \fill[MaterialBlue] ({2+0.3*\x},{\y*1+0.5}) circle[radius=2.5pt];  
            }
            % bundle the 1s
            \draw[dashed,rounded corners,MaterialRed900] (6.1,0.3) -- (7.4,0.3) -- (7.4,1.7) -- (7,1.7) -- (7,0.8) -- (6.1,0.8) -- cycle; 
            \draw[dashed,rounded corners,MaterialRed900] (6.1,1.3) -- (6.1,2.7) -- (7.4,2.7) -- (7.4,1.8) -- (6.45,1.8) -- (6.45,1.3) -- cycle; 
            \foreach \y in {0,2} {
              \fill[MaterialRed900](5.5,{\y+0.5}) circle[radius=2.5pt];
              \draw[->] (6.1,{\y+0.5}) -- (5.6,{\y+0.5}); 
            }
            % cross out the ones:
            \foreach \y in {0,1,2} {
              \foreach \x in {1,4} \draw[thick] ({6+0.3*\x-0.1},{\y+0.4}) -- ({6+0.3*\x+0.1},{\y+0.6});
            }
            \foreach \y in {0,2} {
              \foreach \x in {2,3} \draw[thick] ({6+0.3*\x-0.1},{\y+0.4}) -- ({6+0.3*\x+0.1},{\y+0.6});
            }
            % bundle the fives:
            \draw[dashed,rounded corners, MaterialRed900] (4.1,0.2) -- (4.1,2.8) -- (5.7,2.8) -- (5.7,2.3) -- (4.45,2.3) -- (4.45,0.2) -- cycle; 
            \fill[MaterialRed900] (3.5,1.5) circle[radius=2.5pt];
            \draw[->] (4.1,1.5) -- (3.6,1.5);
            % cross out the fives
            \foreach \x in {1,2,5} \draw[thick] ({4+0.3*\x-0.1},2.4) -- ({4+0.3*\x+0.1},2.6);
            \foreach \y in {0,1} {
            \foreach \x in {1} \draw[thick] ({4+0.3*\x-0.1},{\y+0.4}) -- ({4+0.3*\x+0.1},{\y+0.6});
            }
            % bundle the 25s:
            \draw[dashed,rounded corners, MaterialRed900] (2.1,1.2) -- (2.1,2.8) -- (3.1,2.8) -- (3.1,2.3) -- (2.7,2.3) -- (2.7,1.2) -- cycle; 
            \draw[dashed,rounded corners, MaterialRed900] (2.1,0.1) -- (3.7,0.1) -- (3.7,1.7) -- (2.7,1.7) -- (2.7,0.7) -- (2.1,0.7) -- cycle;
            \foreach \y in {0,1} {
              \fill[MaterialRed900] (1.5,{\y+0.5}) circle[radius=2.5pt];
              \draw[->] (2.1,{\y+0.5}) -- (1.6,{\y+0.5});
            }
            % cross out the 25s
            \foreach \y in {0,1,2}
            \foreach \x in {1,2,3} \draw[thick] ({2+0.3*\x-0.1},{\y+0.4}) -- ({2+0.3*\x+0.1},{\y+0.6});
            \foreach \y in {1} {
            \foreach \x in {5} \draw[thick] ({2+0.3*\x-0.1},{\y+0.4}) -- ({2+0.3*\x+0.1},{\y+0.6});
            }
            \end{tikzpicture}
          ]]>
          </latex-image>
        </image>

        <p>
          and the result is 2 fiftoons, 0 quarters, 3 nickels and 2 pennies or <m>2032_{5}</m>.
        </p>

        <p>
          We can also find the product using the column algorithm.
          Pull out the multiplication table that you made.
          We'll use the expanded version to make things a bit easier:
          <me>
            \begin{array}{rrrrrl} \amp\amp3 \amp 2 \amp 4\amp  \\ \times\amp\amp  \amp \amp 3 \amp \\ \hline \amp\amp\amp2\amp 2  \amp \to 3 \times 4 \\ \amp\amp1 \amp 1 \amp 0 \amp\to 3\times 20 \\ \amp1\amp4 \amp 0 \amp 0 \amp\to 3\times 300 \\ \hline \amp 2\amp 0 \amp 3 \amp 2 \end{array}
          </me>
        </p>

        <p>
          where the only bundling in this case needed to occur in the third column (25s) in which 5 twenty-fives became a 125.
        </p>
      </solution>
    </example>
  </subsection>
</section>